okf_version: "1.0"
task: "User: 또 ImportSession mcp가 클로드, 코덱스 기타 등등의 cli runtime들에서 전혀 동작하지 않아 (ImportSession does not work in Claude, Codex or other CLI runtimes)."
what_it_is: "ImportSession is a Ciel request shortcut, not an MCP server: routed launches install slash commands (Claude Code: ~/.claude/commands/ImportSession.md, Codex: ~/.codex/prompts/ImportSession.md) whose body carries the CIEL_RUNTIME_IMPORT_SESSION marker; the router intercepts the request whose latest user text holds that marker and answers with a Claude/Codex transcript. It only works while the session's model traffic goes through the router (routed mode); native sessions (provider=anthropic native, provider=codex ChatGPT, native agy) never reach Ciel."
router_side_verified: "Isolated router, both wires: POST /v1/responses with the marker returned a streaming answer 'Ciel Runtime ImportSession completed. - current client: codex - transcript: C:\\Users\\djlov\\.codex\\sessions\\2026\\09\\10\\rollout-...' (200); POST /v1/messages likewise streamed a response. The intercept is wired into both the Responses and the Claude router assemblies."
root_cause: "The user's Claude Code command files were gone: C:\\Users\\djlov\\.claude\\commands was empty with LastWriteTime 2026-09-18 14:33:10. A native-mode launch removes the shared assets (install_ciel_runtime_slash_commands for routed launches, disable_ciel_runtime_slash_commands_for_native for native ones), and the unit group's headless-update test performs a native launch - launch-state.json records anthropic-native launches at 14:33:24 (temp worktree) and 14:34:16 (this workspace) during that sweep."
damage: "Every Ciel slash command disappeared for the user's profile: ImportSession.md, advisor.md, llm.md, llm-options.md, llm-restore.md, api-key(s).md, channel-clear.md, ciel-version.md, router-debug.md. The Codex prompt survived (~/.codex/prompts/ImportSession.md present)."
root_cause_fix: "runtime_paths.py: CLI_ASSET_HOME = CONFIG_DIR when CIEL_RUNTIME_TEST_ISOLATED, else HOME; CLAUDE_COMMANDS_DIR, CLAUDE_SETTINGS_PATH, CLAUDE_GATEWAY_CACHE and CIEL_RUNTIME_STATUSLINE_PATH derive from it, and ciel_runtime.py passes CLI_ASSET_HOME as the asset home so the Codex prompts directory follows. Isolated installs/removals now cannot reach the user's profile."
repair: "Ran install_ciel_runtime_slash_commands() + install_ciel_runtime_codex_prompts() without isolation: 10 assets rewritten into ~/.claude/commands (ImportSession.md restored) at 20:51; the restored commands are visible to the running session again."
regression_tests: "tests/test_unisolated_test_guard.py::IsolatedCliAssetTests - isolated paths stay inside the config dir (and the plain run still resolves the real ~/.claude/commands, ~/.codex/prompts); isolated install writes inside the isolated dir; isolated native cleanup cannot delete foreign command files. 7 OK."
runtimes_without_assets: "agy, grok, zcode and muse get no import asset today (only Claude commands and the Codex prompt are installed), so there is nothing to invoke there; typing the marker text into a routed session would still trigger the intercept."
verification: "unit 1500, router 1135, channel 406, runtime 296 - all OK; ruff clean."
state: "Working tree, committed; not deployed to the local snapshot."
